      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Difficult to implement without transactioning.  See \n    <span class=\"jira-issue-macro resolved\" data-jira-key=\"FCREPO-842\" >\n                <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-842\" class=\"jira-issue-macro-key issue-link\"  title=\"If a previous &quot;add&quot; to the policy index (dbxml) fails, subsequent updates fail as the existing doc can&#39;t be deleted\" >\n            <img class=\"icon\" src=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/2/universal_avatar/view/type/issuetype/avatar/10303?size=medium\" />\n            FCREPO-842\n        </a>\n                                                    <span class=\"aui-lozenge aui-lozenge-subtle aui-lozenge-success jira-macro-single-issue-export-pdf\">Closed</span>\n            </span>\n instead, which is for the safest way of handling this - ie changes always get committed to the datastream, even if the DBXML indexing fails (handle policy index add/update/delete in a \"safe\" way)</p>",
     "created": "20/Dec/10 12:57 PM",
     "id": "11744",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10771/comment/11744",
