    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/ddfaabcc9635974ebed182e89941a947?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSB-2.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Stephen Bayliss",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Reopening - thinking again on this, it would be useful to do policy validation (if enabled) on the xacml before we attempt the datastream modification, and fail the api call at that point - ie if attempting to add/modify datastream to invalid XACML then the datastream should not be modified.</p>\n\n<p>This will mean looking at where the validation takes place - currently it's in the dbxml update layer; it should be further up the stack, with the validation removed from the lower levels.</p>\n\n<p>However existing behaviour - if the dbxml update for some (other) reason fails, this should not prevent further updates to the policy index, and the datastream update should succeed - that's the fix already committed; though currently provoked by the lower-level xacml validation exception.</p>",
     "created": "03/Jan/11 8:58 PM",
     "id": "11751",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/10771/comment/11751",
     "updateAuthor": {
      "accountId": "6089a4cb543264006867626e",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": true,
